          "source_quote": "κατὰ τὴν σεμνότητα τοῦ Θεοῦ",
          "english_quote": "‘Solemnity for God’ (subjective genitive)",
          "issue": "The theological metadata mislabels its proposed God-directed alternative as a subjective genitive: “for God” makes God the object or recipient of the solemnity, not its subject. Moreover, this explicitly recorded interpretive alternative is absent from reader-facing footnote d, which lists lexical alternatives and version differences but not the alternative interpretation required by project policy.",
          "suggested_revision": "Reassess whether the God-directed alternative is sufficiently supported to retain. If retained, describe its grammatical relationship accurately and disclose it in footnote d; if withdrawn, correct the metadata with a source-based explanation. Any new English wording needs fresh review.",
