          "issue": "The theological metadata cites an “elect” entry absent from the supplied current policy and claims an unsupported project default. It also records “Render as God’s elect” as the chosen reading, although this edition actually uses “God’s chosen people.” Both English expressions can represent the source, but the audit metadata does not accurately identify this edition’s decision.",
          "suggested_revision": "Record “God’s chosen people” as this edition’s chosen rendering, explain its relationship to ἐκλεκτοῖς, and remove the nonexistent policy-table citation and unsupported default claim.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "κατὰ τὴν σεμνότητα τοῦ Θεοῦ",
          "english_quote": "‘Solemnity for God’ (subjective genitive)",
          "issue": "The proposed God-directed alternative is incorrectly classified as subjective rather than object-directed. The simplified edition’s reader-facing footnote d also omits this interpretive alternative even though its theological metadata retains it, contrary to the policy requiring reader-facing disclosure of retained theological alternatives.",
          "suggested_revision": "Reassess the alternative against the Greek. If retained, accurately describe the relationship and add a concise disclosure to footnote d; otherwise document its withdrawal rather than continuing to list it as a supported alternative. Review any replacement wording independently.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Both editions independently cover the selected Greek’s clauses, roles, actions, questions, positive evil assertion, repeated repentance conditions, construction deadline, denial of a place, and exclusion without adding doctrinal conditions. Contextual “repent” and the service terminology comply with current policy. The witness notes are compatible with the supplied attributed reports and distinguish corrections, restorations, and mediated evidence without requiring replacement of the working reading. Minor revisions are needed to inaccurate policy and interpretive metadata and to disclosure of the retained theological alternative. This review does not authenticate unseen manuscripts, editions, or handwriting."
